# gdlint configuration for Sword and Planet.
#
# Only the keys below are overridden; every other rule keeps gdtoolkit's
# default, so this file does not freeze the rest of the ruleset in place.
#
# max-file-lines: raised from gdtoolkit's default of 1000.
#
# History matters here, because this key is the one that keeps going red.
# It was raised to 1200 in #230, when rules/core/moba_combatant.gd crossed
# 1000 and was the only file in the project above the default. By #240 the
# combatant was at 1180 and rules/tests/cast_cancel_test.gd at 1197 -- three
# lines of headroom -- so any pull request touching either failed GDScript
# Lint on arrival. max-file-lines is in LINT_NO_IN_FILE_FIX_RULES, so
# gdscript-lint.yml cannot self-heal it: the check goes straight to red and
# waits for a human.
#
# The answer was to split, not to raise again. MobaCrowdControlTracker came
# out of the combatant, channel_test.gd out of cast_cancel_test.gd, and
# shield_test.gd out of sustain_test.gd. The largest .gd file in the project
# is now the combatant at 958, and every file has at least 242 lines of
# headroom.
#
# The threshold stays at 1200 rather than returning to gdtoolkit's 1000
# precisely because the combatant is at 958: dropping to the default would
# leave the one file that grows in almost every rules task with 42 lines of
# room, which is the cliff this split just removed.
#
# When a file next approaches 1200, split it. Raising this number again
# trades a bounded refactor for a few more tasks of runway and puts the
# same failure back on someone else's pull request.
#
# It did approach 1200 -- it landed exactly on it. The combatant grew from
# 958 back to 1200 in five days (#242, #263, #265, #313, #321), so #321 had
# to extract MobaPredictionLedger and trim comment blocks purely to fit, and
# the next task to touch the file (#327, position history) had nowhere to put
# a three-line member. That is the failure this note predicted.
#
# #325 was filed for the split and taken in the #327 pull request, because
# #327 could not land without it. Four collaborators came out, following the
# established Moba* pattern: MobaDamageResolver (the apply_damage pipeline),
# MobaActivationGate (can_activate/commit_activate), MobaStatCache (the
# modifier bonus cache behind get_stat), and MobaCrowdControlTracker gained
# can_perform_action(). The combatant is 1081, with 119 lines of headroom.
#
# That is real headroom but short of the ~240 this file asked for in #249.
# The rest of the decomposition is the facade: ~66 public methods, most of
# them one-line forwards to collaborators that already exist, with roughly
# 200 call sites between the crowd-control and cast/channel/toggle groups.
# Removing those forwarders is the change that would both drop the line
# count properly and retire the max-public-methods suppression, and it is
# too large to ride along with an unrelated feature. It stays open on #325.
#
# The threshold still does not move.
max-file-lines: 1200
